<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    {#
    Versioned jsDelivr npm paths, replacing unversioned
    gstatic/external_hosted URLs, so an archived report keeps rendering the
    same way months later instead of silently changing -- or breaking, if the
    unversioned path is retired -- when the hosted libraries change upstream.
    These are the URLs the Vega project itself documents.

    Versions are taken from the installed Altair, not guessed:
      vega-lite 6.4.1  -- `altair.vegalite.v6.display.VEGALITE_VERSION`, and
                          the `$schema` the generated specs actually carry.
      vega-embed 7.0.2 -- pinned in Altair's own bundled `jupyter/js/index.js`.
      vega 6           -- major only. Altair declares `VEGA_VERSION == "6"`
                          and names no patch, and major is the right pinning
                          level here anyway: Vega-Lite 6 compiles to the Vega
                          6 spec, so compatibility is a major-version
                          contract. Inventing a patch number nobody verified
                          would risk a 404, which fails silently -- the
                          scripts simply do not load and no chart renders.

    Subresource Integrity hashes are not set: computing them means fetching
    the files, which needs network access this build does not have. A fully
    self-contained, offline-renderable report would mean vendoring these
    three files into the repo rather than loading them from a CDN at all --
    a bigger change than pinning, and not done here.
    #}
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@6"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@6.4.1"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@7.0.2"></script>
    <title>
      {{ title }}
    </title>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Google+Sans:400,500,700&amp;subset=cyrillic,cyrillic-ext,latin-ext"
          rel="stylesheet" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/icon?family=Material+Icons+Outlined"
          rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
      {% include "style.css" ignore missing %}
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="header">
      <div class="logo">
        {% include "logo.html" ignore missing %}
      </div>
      <div class="title">
        {{ title }}
      </div>
    </div>

    {% if start_date is defined and start_date %}
      {% include "chips.html.jinja" %}
    {% endif %}

    <cards>
      {# Each card is laid out in a grid. See; .card display layout. #}
      {% for card in cards %} {# each `card` is a pre-rendered HTML #}
        {{ card }}
      {% endfor %}
    </cards>
  </body>
</html>